<div style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; max-width: 900px; margin: auto;">

    ## <h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center; padding: 10px; border: 2px solid #1a5276; border-radius: 8px;">Lesson Planner – Theme # 4 – Lesson # 4</h2>
    <p style="text-align: center; font-style: italic;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>

    ## <h2 style="color: #1a5276;">SECTION 2 — LESSON IDENTIFICATION TABLE</h2>
    <table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
      <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
      </tr>
      <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 8th Grade (CEFR: A2.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> The Environment and Recycling</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> In the Past, People Didn't Recycle as Much as They Do Now.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
      </tr>
      <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
          <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write a short report on a class activity. Interactive: Edit classmates' narratives for clarity and coherence.</p>
          <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a short report about a class recycling activity, describing how practices have changed over time (e.g., "Before, people didn't recycle as much, but now we separate items for recycling.")<br>Can edit for clarity a peer's story about recycling (e.g., "Add more details about the report on the class activity.")<br>Can compose a short description of actions to help the environment (e.g., "We should recycle paper and plastic.").</p>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>

    ## <h2 style="color: #1a5276;">SECTION 3 — AOA STAGES TABLE</h2>
    <table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
      <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
          <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 35%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
          <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
          <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 15%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h4>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification. This stage activates prior knowledge and introduces the lesson's language focus through clear demonstrations.</p>
          </td>
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays two contrasting images: one of a traditional landfill or a street with unseparated trash from the past, and another of a modern recycling center or separated waste bins. Students are asked to briefly describe what they see and how things are different. The teacher writes key words on the board: <i>recycle, waste, environment, pollution</i>. Teacher initiates a quick class discussion: "What did people do with trash 50 years ago? What do we do now?"</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models sentences contrasting past and present recycling practices, emphasizing the grammar structures (Past simple vs. present practices) and pronunciation of past tense verb endings. For example, the teacher writes and says: "In the past, people <b>didn't recycle</b> plastic." (pointing to the image) "Today, we <b>separate</b> plastic bottles." The teacher then writes and says, "They <b>wasted</b> a lot of resources." (focusing on /ɪd/ in 'wasted'). "Now, we <b>save</b> resources." (focusing on /d/ in 'saved'). Teacher models: "If we <b>don't recycle</b>, there <b>will be</b> more pollution."</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
            <ul>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did people often separate paper for recycling 50 years ago, or do they do it more frequently today?" (Checking understanding of past vs. present practices)</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say 'We should protect our planet,' am I telling you something important to do or something optional?" (Checking understanding of modal 'should')</li>
            </ul>
          </td>
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h4>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "The Environment and Recycling". Students observe and process new linguistic elements in context.</p>
          </td>
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short narrative report (approx. 80-100 words) describing a hypothetical school recycling activity conducted in the past and how it would be improved today. The report uses the target grammar (Past simple vs. present practices, First conditional, Modal 'should') and vocabulary (<i>recycle, waste, environment, pollution, energy, landfill, planet, resource, reduce, reuse, clean, save, protect, important</i>).</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Example Report Snippet:</i> "Last year, our class tried to recycle, but we <b>didn't separate</b> items carefully. We just put all plastic and paper in one bin. There <b>was</b> a lot of <b>waste</b>. Today, we know better. We <b>should separate</b> plastic, paper, and glass. If we <b>do this</b>, we <b>will save</b> more <b>resources</b> and reduce <b>pollution</b>. It's <b>important</b> to change our practices."</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Contrasting past and present practices; Expressing cause-effect; Giving advice in written form.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
            <ul>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the report silently. Then, the teacher asks gist questions: "What is the report about?" "What is the main problem it describes?"</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">True/False Activity: Students read statements about the report and mark them T or F (e.g., "Last year, the class separated plastic, paper, and glass carefully." T/F).</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Underline all the verbs in past simple and circle all the 'should' and 'if...will' structures in the text.</li>
            </ul>
          </td>
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h4>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing. Students practice new language components through controlled and semi-controlled activities, building confidence and precision.</p>
          </td>
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Writing sentences with Past simple versus present practices; First conditional (cause-effect); Modal 'should' (giving advice). Vocabulary: <i>recycle, waste, environment, pollution, energy, landfill, planet, resource, reduce, reuse, clean, save, protect, environmental, clean, renewable, important, carefully, often</i>.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
            <ul>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 3.1 (Controlled Practice - Gap Fill):</b> Students receive a worksheet with sentences about environmental practices. They complete the sentences using the correct past simple or present tense verb forms, or 'should' / 'shouldn't', or the correct form for first conditional.
                <br><i>Example:</i> "In the past, people ____ (not reuse) plastic bags, but now we ____ (reuse) them." "If we ____ (save) water, we ____ (protect) the planet." "You ____ (turn off) the lights when you leave the room."</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 3.2 (Semi-controlled - Sentence Building):</b> Students are given sentence starters and a list of vocabulary words. They write complete sentences describing contrasting past/present actions, giving advice, or stating cause-effect.
                <br><i>Example Prompts:</i> "Before, we...", "Now, we should...", "If people...", "We need to protect..."
                <br><i>Vocabulary List:</i> <i>recycle, waste, environment, pollution, energy, landfill, clean, save, protect, important</i>.</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 3.3 (Pair Check - Sentence Correction):</b> In pairs, students exchange their sentences from Activity 3.2. They check each other's sentences for correct grammar (past/present contrast, 'should', first conditional), appropriate vocabulary, and clarity. They underline any errors and suggest corrections. This promotes peer collaboration and sociolinguistic competence in problem-solving.</li>
            </ul>
          </td>
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h4>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "The Environment and Recycling". Focus is on fluency and communicative task completion.</p>
          </td>
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task: Writing a Class Recycling Report</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work individually or in small groups (3-4 students) to write a short report (approx. 70-100 words) about a hypothetical or real class recycling activity. The report should:</p>
            <ul>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Describe how the class <b>didn't recycle</b> or recycled differently <b>in the past</b> (e.g., "Before, we often wasted paper because we didn't have a recycling bin.").</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Explain current recycling practices and awareness <b>today</b> (e.g., "Now, we carefully separate plastic and paper for recycling.").</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Include advice using 'should' (e.g., "We <b>should protect</b> our <b>environment</b> by reducing <b>waste</b>.")</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Include a cause-effect statement using the first conditional (e.g., "If we <b>recycle</b> more, there <b>will be</b> less <b>pollution</b>.").</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use at least 5-7 target vocabulary words (<i>recycle, waste, environment, pollution, energy, landfill, planet, resource, reduce, reuse, clean, save, protect, environmental, clean, important, carefully, often</i>).</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Teacher circulates, providing support and encouraging the use of target structures and vocabulary. Emphasize expressing contrasting past and present practices and giving advice, promoting sociolinguistic competence by proposing solutions.</p>
          </td>
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h4>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy. Students review their work and peers' work against criteria, fostering self-correction and critical thinking.</p>
          </td>
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task: Peer Editing & Self-Correction</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students exchange their written reports with a classmate. Using a simple peer-editing checklist provided by the teacher, they review each other's reports. The checklist includes:</p>
            <ul>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is there a clear contrast between past and present practices? (e.g., "Before, we didn't... / Now, we...")</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is 'should' used correctly to give advice?</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is the first conditional used to show cause-effect?</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are at least 5 target vocabulary words used?</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is the report clear and easy to understand? (clarity and coherence)</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Suggestions for improvement (e.g., "Add more details about how you save energy.")</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students then take back their own reports and make revisions based on peer feedback. Teacher collects the revised reports for final review.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer on a small slip of paper:</p>
            <ul>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new thing I learned about writing about recycling is..."</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One action I *should* take to help the environment is..."</li>
            </ul>
          </td>
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">8 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h4>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students and teacher reflect on the lesson's effectiveness, identifying areas of success and opportunities for growth.</p>
          </td>
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
            <ul>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing the report was most challenging for me, and why?"</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did giving or receiving feedback help me improve my writing about the environment?"</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
            <ul>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this writing lesson? (e.g., scaffolding of grammar practice, peer editing effectiveness, student engagement with the theme).</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for students to further improve their written production for next lesson? (e.g., more sentence starters for lower-proficiency students, explicit modeling of linking words for coherence).</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> The next lesson (Lesson 5: Mediation & Integration) will build on these written reports. Students will mediate information from their reports to create a larger class presentation or project on "Our School's Environmental Footprint: Past, Present, and Future Actions," integrating the 21st Century Skills Project.</p>
          </td>
          <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">7 min</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>